# CBP (Commit → Build → Push TF)

When the user says **CBP** (alone or “do CBP”), run this sequence without re-asking what it means:

1. **Commit** — only the relevant change set (conventional message); push git to the tracked remote after commit (Insite default unless they said not to).
2. **Build** — local PROD iOS path: `./build-local.sh ios production` (auto-bumps shared build number). Use `./build-and-submit.sh ios production true` only when interactive confirm is handled / non-interactive submit follows.
3. **Push to TF** — `npx eas submit --platform ios --path <latest .eas/artifacts/*.ipa> --profile production --non-interactive`. Confirm IPA identity (CFBundleVersion, PROD Supabase bake) before/after submit.
4. **Record** — update `documentation/NOW.md` + ASC paste notes if this binary is the App Store candidate; commit/push that chore bump if `app.json` changed.

Default profile = **production** (App Store / PROD TF) unless the user says DEV / Internal (`./build-local.sh ios dev` + `--profile dev`).

Do not tick Public or Submit for Review unless explicitly asked.
